  "body": "## Why\n\nThe maintainer wrote (2026-11-17): \"WCS54, X flipped - posting and generating are refused until the flip is cleared..  the ability to flip axis from a positive to negative is fundamental and should not be blocked.. posting and generation should take it into consideration rather..\"\n\nThe maintainer decided on 2026-11-18, after the floor review: keep the meaning as built (the machine control runs a flipped axis reversed), and refuse probing in a flipped setup with a message that names the flip.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Generation, verification and the stock simulation no longer refuse a flipped setup. They stay in the setup frame, so the cut does not change.\n- The job writes `PARAM WcsFlip` on each section of a flipped setup. A new post pass (`crates/post/src/post/wcs_flip.rs`) runs before `wcs_rotate` and `invert`. It mirrors the flipped axis about the work origin through `invert::translate_rules`.\n- One flipped axis swaps G2/G3 and G41/G42. Two flipped axes (X and Y) keep them. Helix and canned cycles are carried.\n- The flip composes with a machine-inverted axis.\n- The travel check, the setup sheet and the viewport work envelope read the posted sign.\n- `fanuc.cps` and `haas.cps` state `axisInversion = true` and name the flipped axes in the program header.\n- Review fix (finding 2): a probe operation in a flipped setup is refused by name. The verification gate (`setup_wcs_flip::op_problem`) names the flipped axes and the probe operations. The post pass (`post::wcs_flip`) refuses a flipped section that holds probe records, so each stream builder is covered.\n- Review fix (finding 4): the `refused` field of the MCP `set_wcs_flip` reply also names the operations of the setup that the post refuses (`setup_wcs_flip::setup_post_problems`).\n- Review fix (finding 3): the WCS page note says that the machine control must run the flipped axis reversed, and that probing does not post. The status line names the refusal in place of \"mirrored\" when the post refuses the flip. The page note does not yet read the refusal of a rotated WCS or an unverified post: follow-up #2497 (the note must not load the post script each frame).\n\n## Cases\n\nCarried: Flip X, Flip Y, and Flip X+Y on 3-axis mill sections, with Fanuc and Haas.\n\nRefused by name, with the flip as the cause:\n\n- a flipped Z (follow-up #2474)\n- a script without `axisInversion = true` (follow-up #2475)\n- a flip together with a WCS rotation (follow-up #2476)\n- probing (the maintainer's decision of 2026-11-18)\n- turning, threading, live tool, ABC/tilt, EDM, wire and plasma sections\n- a section that uses a modal origin or start across a change of flip\n- a `WcsFlip` value that the pass cannot read\n\nThe decision file `docs/decisions/1649-wcs-flip-carry.md` has the case table and the reasons. Its new section \"Probing in a flipped setup\" records the probing decision and the dropped option (mirrored probing).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nHeadless renders (egui_kittest, wgpu, 320 x 900) of the WCS page after a click on Flip Y. \"Before\" uses the UI files of `origin/main`. No GUI process was started.\n\n| Before (origin/main) | After (this branch) |\n|---|---|\n| ![WCS page before](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-2492/wcs-flip-note-before.png?raw=true) | ![WCS page after](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-2492/wcs-flip-note-after.png?raw=true) |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/post/tests/wcs_flip.rs` (15 tests), for example `a_flipped_wcs_cuts_the_cam_path`, `one_flipped_axis_reverses_arcs_and_the_compensation_side_and_two_do_not`, `a_flipped_axis_on_an_inverted_machine_axis_posts_the_standard_signs`, `a_flipped_z_refuses_by_name`, `a_flipped_and_rotated_section_refuses_by_name`. New: `probing_in_a_flipped_wcs_refuses_by_name`, `probing_without_a_flip_posts_unchanged`.\n- `crates/app/tests/wcs_flip_post.rs` (10 tests), for example `a_flipped_x_or_y_posts_the_mirrored_program_and_clearing_it_posts_as_before`, `generation_runs_in_a_flipped_setup_and_the_toolpath_does_not_change`. New: `probing_in_a_flipped_setup_refuses_the_post_by_name` (also asserts `setup_post_problems`), `probing_in_an_unflipped_setup_posts_unchanged`.\n- `crates/app/tests/wcs_flip.rs` (7 tests), with `the_mcp_tool_sets_the_flags_and_get_job_shows_them`.\n- `crates/ui` `wcs_flip_tests` (4 tests). New: `the_status_line_names_a_flip_that_the_post_refuses`.\n\n## Gate\n\nHead `7c319cb26af2c9d57859b63591607896ffced3b7` (merge of `origin/main` b48c65828 into the branch). Quick gate `gate-logs/quick-20261118-112811` with `--base origin/main`: 641 steps, 639 ok, 2 red. The two red steps are red on main and are tracked by #2483:\n\n- `app suites: microarc_test_part` (`a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a`, Tormach wrap golden)\n- `app suites: stock_source_holes` (`framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number`, from #2450)\n\nClippy (`-p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`) has one error: `crates/app/src/operation/heights.rs:128`, which is on main and tracked by #2479. With that one lint allowed, clippy is clean.\n\nThe merge of `origin/main` had one conflict, in `crates/app/src/setup_sheet/sections.rs`: this branch added the flip line and main added the origin line (#870) at the same place. The two lines are kept.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The other post scripts (they refuse until #2475 verifies them).\n- A real controller.\n- Lathe and multi-axis programs (they refuse by name).\n- The real GUI window. The screenshots are headless renders.\n\n## Labels and notes\n\nEffort: max. The issue did not escalate.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nThe process change is one row in the `camcraft-mcp` skill (`set_wcs_flip`: the `refused` field names the refused operations).\n\nChangelog: A setup's Flip X / Flip Y no longer refuses generation and the post: Fanuc and Haas programs mirror the flipped axis, with the arc direction and compensation side kept correct. A flipped Z, a probe operation in a flipped setup, and the other post scripts still refuse by name.\n\nFixes #1649\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
